      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Modem version of I. Mechnikov's hypothesis on association of somatic diseases with infectious agents is presented. List of bacteria and viruses associated with various types of cardiomyopathies, atherosclerosis, gastritis, gastric and duodenal ulcerative disease, type 1 diabetes mellitus. Literature data showing that influenza vaccination reduces number of fatal myocardial infarctions and strokes during winter seasons as well as number of hospitalizations due to exacerbations of chronic cardiovascular and cerebrovascular diseases are summarized. Data on probability of coincidence of influenza vaccination and sudden death in elderly persons are reviewed."},
